  "body": "There should be an option to treat unspecified parts as wildcard instead of an empty string. For example, the current behaviour:\r\n```\r\n> new URLPattern(\"https://example.com\")\r\nURLPattern {\r\n  protocol: \"https\",\r\n  username: \"\",\r\n  password: \"\",\r\n  hostname: \"example.com\",\r\n  port: \"\",\r\n  pathname: \"/\",\r\n  search: \"\",\r\n  hash: \"\"\r\n}\r\n```\r\nwhat i would like:\r\n```\r\n> new URLPattern(\"https://example.com\", { defaultToWindcard: true })\r\nURLPattern {\r\n  protocol: \"https\",\r\n  username: \"*\",\r\n  password: \"*\",\r\n  hostname: \"example.com\",\r\n  port: \"*\",\r\n  pathname: \"/\",\r\n  search: \"*\",\r\n  hash: \"*\"\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe one problem I see however is the fact that pathname still would default to `\"/\"`",
